# The Continuous Compliance Loop

The Vyra architecture is organized around a single operating model.

```text
Regulations
→ Requirements
→ Execution
→ Operations
→ Signals
→ Reasoning
→ Risk
→ Remediation
→ Assurance
→ Trust
```

This lifecycle is called the Continuous Compliance Loop.

Every component within the platform exists to advance information through this loop.

Every graph models a portion of this loop.

Every agent contributes to this loop.

Every service supports this loop.

The loop is both the operating model and the organizing principle of the architecture.

Unlike traditional compliance programs, the loop never stops.

Compliance becomes continuously observable, continuously measurable, and continuously improvable.

